From 92f390aef27f66f18276cb4a82d53c988b559a82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:52:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tcp_bbr3: tolerate a missing private state in cwnd_event

bbr3_init() allocates the per-socket state with GFP_ATOMIC and leaves
the slot NULL when the allocation fails. Every other entry point checks
for that, but bbr3_cwnd_event() dereferences the pointer directly, so a
CA_EVENT_TX_START after an idle period oopses, and GKI panics on oops.
Return early like the other callbacks.
---
 net/ipv4/tcp_bbr3.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/ipv4/tcp_bbr3.c b/net/ipv4/tcp_bbr3.c
index b3868c541..828039719 100644
--- a/net/ipv4/tcp_bbr3.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/tcp_bbr3.c
@@ -471,6 +471,10 @@ static void bbr3_cwnd_event(struct sock *sk, enum tcp_ca_event event)
 	struct tcp_sock *tp = tcp_sk(sk);
 	struct bbr3 *bbr = bbr3_get_priv(sk);
 
+	/* bbr3_init() allocates with GFP_ATOMIC and may fail. */
+	if (!bbr || !bbr->initialized)
+		return;
+
 	if (event == CA_EVENT_TX_START) {
 		if (!tp->app_limited)
 			return;
